{
  "title": "The path that draws itself",
  "duration": 64,
  "outputSize": [1920, 1080],
  "fps": 24,
  "narrationSource": "static/audio/articles/i-have-a-job/UzI1NsMEV3ni5JRkRSls-ac2f6d88d3c9.m4a",
  "narration": [
    {
      "text": "The work is moving. My hands are empty.",
      "start": 5.94,
      "end": 8.88,
      "duration": 2.9400000000000004,
      "timelineStart": 2.9
    },
    {
      "text": "For years, programming gave me a quiet confidence: whatever happens, the craft will feed me. I know something that people need.",
      "start": 45.26,
      "end": 54.08,
      "duration": 8.82,
      "timelineStart": 8.6
    },
    {
      "text": "I use AI every day, and I see how much it helps me. That is exactly why the dependence unsettles me.",
      "start": 58.8,
      "end": 66.4,
      "duration": 7.6000000000000085,
      "timelineStart": 18.2
    },
    {
      "text": "More and more, I am a filter for what AI produces. I get more done without feeling more capable.",
      "start": 107.04,
      "end": 114.02,
      "duration": 6.97999999999999,
      "timelineStart": 27.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The direction is still mine.",
      "start": 115.54,
      "end": 117.12,
      "duration": 1.5799999999999983,
      "timelineStart": 36.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Writing is something I return to on my own, without anyone assigning it to me. I begin with a thought that is not yet clear, and it becomes clearer as I write it down.",
      "start": 273.9,
      "end": 284.78,
      "duration": 10.879999999999995,
      "timelineStart": 39.0
    },
    {
      "text": "While I write, my hands are not empty.",
      "start": 286.0,
      "end": 288.18,
      "duration": 2.180000000000007,
      "timelineStart": 51.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not know what my work will look like in two years. Until then, I want to keep living, writing, and trying.",
      "start": 300.54,
      "end": 308.3,
      "duration": 7.759999999999991,
      "timelineStart": 54.0
    }
  ],
